summary:
  Unsubscribing matches the raw feed string while the star that offers it
  matches feed keys, so a show reached under its other spelling shows a lit
  star whose click removes nothing and says nothing.

history:
  isPodcastSubscribed was loosened to feed keys on 2026-09-06 so that one
  show over http and https, with and without a trailing slash, would be one
  subscription. removePodcastSub was left on ===. Both roads are driven by
  the same button with the same url, so the looser test lit the star and the
  stricter one refused to clear it — a show found again through search could
  not be unsubscribed at all. The old bug subscribed twice; this one never
  lets go. Found 2026-09-08, before the release that introduced it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/PodcastEngine.qml

find:
              if (PodcastLogic.feedKey(podcastSubsModel.get(i).feedUrl) === want) {
                  podcastSubsModel.remove(i);

replace:
              if (podcastSubsModel.get(i).feedUrl === feedUrl) {
                  podcastSubsModel.remove(i);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_podcastengine.qml::test_a_twin_spelling_can_also_unsubscribe.
  Line-neutral.
